WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.960
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.360
Today we look at the best
way to treat a condition

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.120
that affects nearly
60 percent of all women.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.320
DHEA supplements
don’t seem to help

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.560
with female sexual dysfunction,

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.960
but what about
other dietary supplements,

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.960
such as the three roots:
ginseng, maca, and ashwagandha?

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.560
Ginseng has been suggested,

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.560
given its demonstrated efficacy
for male erectile dysfunction

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.400
and the fact that it causes
a relaxation response in vitro

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.000
to isolated strips
of rabbit vaginal tissue.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.800
But when put to the test
in human studies,

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.160
a meta-analysis found

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.960
no statistically significant
effect of ginseng

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.520
on female sexual dysfunction.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.600
Maca root has been advertised
as Peruvian Viagra.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.200
It’s an important dietary staple

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.040
of the indigenous people
of Peru

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.360
but appears
to have been overly hyped

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.720
as a libido enhancer

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.520
based largely on studies
of male rodents.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.320
Yes, maca seems to enhance
the sexual function

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.920
of male mice and rats,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.200
but of the two trials
on sexual desire in male humans,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.680
only one showed
a significant benefit,

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.840
but it took eight weeks
to show an effect,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.440
which may explain
the negative results

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.880
of the second study,
which only lasted two weeks.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.520
A pilot study
without a placebo control

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.600
on the management
of sexual dysfunction

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.600
induced by SSRIs (due to drugs
like Prozac or Zoloft)

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.680
on mostly women
suggested maca may be useful,

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.080
but when properly put
to the test in a randomized,

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.400
double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.360
it failed to have
a significant effect.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.520
The necessity of placebos
is illustrated

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.400
by a maca trial
for infertility.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.800
Maca increased
sperm concentration

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.720
by 40 percent!

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.280
Yeah, but the placebo
in the study

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.400
improved sperm concentration
by 76 percent,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.680
so maca didn’t work after all.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.560
Having placebo controls
is particularly important

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.640
for female sexual dysfunction,

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.520
since based on studies
of almost 4,000 women,

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.120
the placebo effect accounts
for more than two-thirds

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.480
of the treatment effect,

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.480
similar to the placebo efficacy
of antidepressants.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.920
In contrast, improvement rates
for erectile dysfunction

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.360
in men given placebos

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.320
are on the order
of 15 percent or less.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.640
The thought is that just the act
of consistent self-monitoring

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.800
in female sexual dysfunction
trials,

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.400
for example by being asked
to keep a symptom diary,

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.320
may improve symptoms
by heightening

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.160
the participant’s attention
and awareness

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.320
of her own responses
and behaviors,

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.280
even in lieu
of an active treatment.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.600
There was one small randomized,
double-blind,

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.200
placebo-controlled trial of maca

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.000
for sexual dysfunction
in postmenopausal women.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.680
Fourteen women
were randomized

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.920
to about 3/4 of a teaspoon
(~4 g) of maca powder

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.800
or a placebo powder
every day for six weeks,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.760
after which point they switched
for another six weeks.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.120
While on the real maca,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.120
they reported
significantly fewer symptoms

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.120
of sexual dysfunction.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.520
Ashwagandha is a revered herb

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.200
of the traditional Indian
Ayurvedic system of medicine.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.920
Its name comes from "ashwa,"
which means horse,

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.120
and "gandha,"
which means smell,

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.720
because the roots
evidently possess

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.560
the "distinctive smell
of a wet horse."

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.000
Ashwagandha is used
as a household remedy in India

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.840
where it’s been considered
a rasayana, a "rejuvenator,"

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.080
or "tonic,"
for thousands of years,

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.280
earning it the nickname
of Indian ginseng.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.440
After being fed the root,

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.840
rodents thrown
into the deep end

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.800
swim twice as long
before sinking

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.320
(12 hours versus 6 hours).

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.160
Benefits for
physical performance

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.240
(including an increase
in aerobic fitness)

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.120
have been found in people too.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.120
One study demonstrated evidence
of cognitive benefits as well.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.160
Its Latin name,

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.880
Withania somnifera
points to another use

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.200
(somnifera means
"sleep-inducer").

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.680
A meta-analysis of five
randomized controlled trials

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.040
of ashwagandha extracts

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.960
found a small
but significant effect

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.200
on overall sleep.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.720
What about ashwagandha
and female sexual dysfunction?

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.520
Women ages 21 thorough 50
were randomized

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.520
to two months
of the estimated equivalent

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.160
of three grams
of ashwagandha root powder

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.520
and did not have
an increase in sexual desire,

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.720
but they did show improvements
over placebo in arousal,

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.680
lubrication, orgasm,
and satisfaction,

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.040
translating into an additional

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.920
quote-unquote
"successful sexual encounter"

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.160
by the end of the study.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.760
What are the downsides?

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.640
Ashwagandha belongs
to the nightshade family,

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.760
which includes some
shady characters like tobacco

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.720
and, well,
deadly nightshade.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:01.760
There have been rare cases

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:05.040
of ashwagandha-linked
liver toxicity reported,

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.720
though commercial
herbal supplements

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.920
are often mislabeled,

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.360
so it’s hard to definitively
attribute certain cases.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.840
However, there have been
several liver injury cases

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.920
in which the supplements
have been tested

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.760
and found to be
contaminant-free,

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.320
suggesting that ashwagandha-
induced liver toxicity

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.080
is a real phenomenon,
however rare.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.680
What should we expect
from a plant

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.680
known by its other nickname,
poison gooseberry.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.200
Did you know that the buildup
of cholesterol in pelvic arteries

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.120
can lead to sexual problems
among both men and women

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.360
via a similar pathway?

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.960
Here’s the story.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.640
Cholesterol doesn’t just build up
inside our coronary arteries;

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.840
it builds up inside
all of our arteries.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.560
In the heart,
it can cause a heart attack.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.280
In the brain,
it can cause a stroke.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:58.080
In our legs, it can cause
peripheral vascular disease.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:03.040
And clogs in our pelvic arteries
can lead to sexual dysfunction—

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.560
and not just in men.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:11.600
“Hyperlipidemia and sexual function
in premenopausal women.”

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.080
Those with high cholesterol “reported

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:19.680
significantly lower arousal, orgasm,
lubrication, and satisfaction.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:25.200
Atherosclerosis of the arterial bed
supplying female pelvic anatomy

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.520
can lead to decreased vaginal engorgement

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.880
and clitoral erectile
insufficiency syndrome,

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.200
similar to erectile problems in men,

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.520
resulting in vasculogenic
female sexual dysfunction,”

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:41.840
an important factor of which may be
failure to achieve “clitoral tumescence,”

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.840
or engorgement.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:51.280
Eating healthier can extend one’s life
and also one’s love life.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:52.560
In our final story today,

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.600
we look at dietary approaches
to female sexual dysfunction.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.760
The creation and promotion of

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.080
“female sexual dysfunction”
as a mental disorder seems

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.800
like a textbook case of disease-mongering

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:09.360
by the pharmaceutical industry harkening

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:13.200
back to the first DSM,
psychiatry’s diagnosis manual,

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.480
which listed frigidity as a mental disorder,

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.600
along, of course, with homosexuality.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.080
The latest manifestation is hypoactive

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.760
sexual desire disorder,

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.880
a disease invented by drug companies.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.840
It’s like when Prozac was
about to go off patent,

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.440
the company sponsored the creation

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.440
of new mental illness to market

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.440
a drug called Sarafem,

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.680
which was simply Prozac repacked

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.920
into a pink capsule.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.600
The condition previously known

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.920
as shyness was branded as

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:45.520
“social anxiety disorder;”

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.800
so they could get kids on Paxil.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:52.400
There are certainly women
who are troubled by low libido,

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.120
but there is no reliable
scientific evidence that

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.120
hypoactive sexual desire disorder

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.440
is a real medical condition.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.840
And, women can get
diagnosed with it

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.560
even with a normal libido.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.720
A woman highly interested in sex,

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.360
just not (for whatever reason)
with her current partner,

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:13.920
can still qualify for the
diagnosis—and the drug.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.240
Even a woman who is perfectly satisfied

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.320
with her sex life may still
qualify if her partner isn’t.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:24.240
Our story begins in 2009,
when a drug company tried

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.320
to get a failed antidepressant
called Flibanserin approved

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.360
to treat hypoactive sexual desire disorder.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.040
The only problem...?

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.480
It didn’t work.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.720
It was resubmitted again after more study,

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.800
and was still rejected, as was the appeal.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.880
But, in 2015, the FDA approved the drug.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.000
What changed?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.840
Nothing about its efficacy;

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.120
it didn’t work any better.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:50.960
What changed is that the drug company

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.720
that bought it helped launch

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.160
an astroturf fake grassroots
advocacy group,

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.640
“Even the Score,” which lobbied

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.520
for approval under a feminist rubric.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.120
Men have their drugs;

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.240
why don’t women get any sex drugs,

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.800
which was exposed as
kind of a bitter irony.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:12.080
But hey, within 48 hours of FDA approval,

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:16.160
the drug was sold for
a cool billion in cash.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.880
Very satisfying for the drug company,

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:20.320
but what about the women

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.680
who take the drug

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.880
(now sold as Addyi)?

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.480
Not much.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:30.880
The drug just doesn’t work as advertised.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.640
Yes, it may stimulate monkeys

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:33.920
to groom each other more.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.760
But, when researchers dug up

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.320
the unpublished data about the drug,

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.840
any clinical benefit was found

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.120
to be marginal,

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.800
and the drug was found to have

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:45.120
significant adverse side effects.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:48.480
Besides being ineffective,
it can be dangerous.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.640
Combining it with alcohol can cause

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:53.120
dangerous hypotension and fainting—

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.640
problems so serious that the FDA
put a black box warning on it,

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.480
its most serious safety alert,

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:01.440
on the label (that of course no one reads).

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:04.560
Even without alcohol,
it can cause severe drops

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.640
in blood pressure levels and cause

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.600
sudden prolonged unconsciousness.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.600
Now, serious side effects

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.400
might be acceptable

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.920
in some kind of cancer

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:14.960
wonder drug or something,

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:18.480
but are entirely unacceptable in a drug

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:19.840
given to healthy women

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.080
for an invented condition.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:25.920
Are there any safe and natural solutions?

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:26.960
Well, there’s lots of studies

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:29.360
on diet and men’s sexual health,

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:30.960
but what about women’s?

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.400
I’ve previously explored the evidence

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.040
about women with high cholesterol levels

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.200
reporting diminished sexual function

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.160
across a number of dimensions.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.640
This could explain why a
more plant-based diet,

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.480
rich in a variety of whole plant foods,

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:46.480
might be effective in ameliorating

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.960
sexual function issues in women,

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.560
as it does in men,

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.560
more whole grains, beans,
vegetables, and fruit,

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.160
and less meat, dairy, and sugar

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:58.320
associated with a reduced risk
of erectile dysfunction,

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.240
because the anatomy and physiology

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:03.120
of sexual responses are actually

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.800
quite similar between the two;

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.400
they can have a similar effect.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.640
You can measure clitoral engorgement

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.280
with fancy MRI techniques within

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.640
minutes of exposure to an erotic video.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:17.680
And, we know now that lubrication

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:20.160
is all about blood flow too.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.160
Within the sexually aroused vagina,

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:23.600
it’s the hydrostatic pressure

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:24.880
from all the additional pelvic

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.560
blood flow that forces fluid

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.640
to leak out onto the surface

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:31.200
as the vaginal lubrication.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.080
So, how can we improve blood flow?

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:36.000
Well, the flavonoid phytonutrients

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.480
in cocoa can help open up arteries,

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.095
increasing pulse wave amplitude

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:43.120
peaking at about 90
minutes after consumption.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.760
So, can that Valentine’s Day chocolate

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.215
make a difference?

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.360
Women who eat chocolate do tend

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.120
to have higher female sexual

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:52.720
function index scores,

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.680
but the effect disappeared once

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.200
age was taken into account.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.680
So, despite all the potential biological

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:01.120
mechanisms supporting a role

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.840
for chocolate as an aphrodisiac food,

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:07.040
the study failed to show a benefit.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:08.880
One would assume that chocolate

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.560
could improve blood flow,

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.520
but remember that was with cocoa powder.

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:14.960
Maybe the fat and sugar in chocolate

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.920
is counteracting the benefits.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.280
What are some whole food
sources of flavonoids?

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:23.520
Well, onions have a lot.

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.640
And indeed, fresh onion juice enhances

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.080
copulatory behavior—in rats,

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.920
but for those of us less interested

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.880
in increasing the percentage
of ejaculating rats,

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.640
and looking for something other

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.440
than onion juice for our hot date,

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:43.120
how about that apple?

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.880
There wasn’t a study addressing

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:46.240
the potential correlation between

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:49.680
daily apple consumption and
women’s sexual function…

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.720
until now.

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.320
The title kind of gives it away,

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:58.160
but women were split into
regular daily apple consumers

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:01.360
versus those consuming less
than an apple a day,

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:05.280
and the hundreds of apple eaters
in the study scored significantly

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:08.960
higher on the female
sexual function index.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:12.960
Now, note they only included women
eating unpeeled apples,

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.600
because the phytonutrients are
concentrated in the peel:

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:18.560
so, we don’t know if there’s a link
with peeled apples.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:23.280
And, this was just an observational study;
so, further studies will be necessary

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:28.000
to clarify the relationship
between apple intake and female sexuality.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:32.480
However, the present data can allow
the “development of future research

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:35.680
for identifying new compounds
and food supplements to use

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:38.080
in female sexuality recovery.”

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:43.600
Uh, or, you can just try
eating an apple.

